    <div style="padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:40px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;max-width:70ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#8A9099;">EVERYTHING ELSE IT DOES</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,46px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">Built for the twenty minutes you are on stage.</h2>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:16px;">
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FF4438;">LOOPING</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Five tracks, quantized both ways</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Launch on immediate, next beat, next bar or next cycle; stop on immediate, end of beat, bar or loop — per track and as a song default. Pre-set lengths to 32 bars, and a fixed recording closes itself.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FFB020;">LAYERS</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Sum or replace, undo on every track</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">SUM keeps every layer, REPLACE overwrites under the pass. One layer of undo and redo per track, independent of the arrangement’s own stack.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#35D07F;">MONITORING</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">You hear yourself immediately</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">Input 1 is audible at launch, everything else starts muted, and nothing has to be armed — or even to exist — for that to be true.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#4CC9F0;">INPUTS</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Pan into the take, stereo links</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">An input’s pan is recorded, not just monitored. Link inputs 1, 3, 5 or 7 to the one after it and the pair becomes one strip with one chain across both channels.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#A78BFA;">YOUR FILES</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Every pass is a WAV you can open</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">32-bit float, two-channel, at your interface’s sample rate, written when the pass closes with no save step. Songs are folders in ~/Music/LOOM.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FF4438;">HARDWARE</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Change interface mid-session</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">No relaunch. Your routing is captured and restored across the change, and LOOM warns you first when a track still holds audio — counting the loss in the heading.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#FFB020;">WHEN IT SPEAKS</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">One notice row, and it remembers</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">The same height whether it holds a two-line refusal or nothing, so nothing on screen moves. LOG opens everything LOOM told you this session, selectable and copyable.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#35D07F;">ACCESSIBILITY</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Keyboard-complete, and it talks</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">A self-test walks the live window and fails the build unless every command control is named and reachable. The notice line and the focused track’s phase are announced, on one switch you can silence for a set.</div>
          </div>
        
          <div style="background:#0F1114;border:1px solid #23262C;border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px 30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:11px;">
            <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:0.18em;color:#4CC9F0;">THE MANUAL</div>
            <div style="font-size:17.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-0.015em;line-height:1.25;">Inside the app, as a PDF</div>
            <div style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#8A9099;text-wrap:pretty;">⌘? opens it. No network call — it is on your machine, so it is there on a stage, behind a captive portal, and at two in the morning.</div>
          </div>
        
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="honest" style="scroll-margin-top:88px;padding:128px 0 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:34px;">
      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;max-width:70ch;">
        <div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.2em;color:#8A9099;">WHAT LOOM DOES NOT HAVE</div>
        <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,46px);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.03em;line-height:1.05;text-wrap:balance;">Read this before you buy it.</h2>
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:17.5px;line-height:1.6;color:#C7CDD4;text-wrap:pretty;">LOOM refuses to draw a control that is wired to nothing, because on stage that reads as a bug. The application ships a manual page listing what is deliberately absent. Here is the same list. Some of these are decisions; some are simply not built yet, and the difference is marked.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:28px 48px;max-width:860px;">
        
